ers were on strike  not so long ago now see strikes amongst  barristers  threatened strikes amongst teachers  amongst other public servants if we're  now facing a summer with a caretaker  government and a contest for a new  leader one of the questions that's going  to have to be resolved is uh to what  extent can public pay be increased  without further stoking inflation  britain has been uh vigorous certainly  not alone in the world of course but  vigorous in supplying ukraine with uh  both weapons and money but also a form  of moral support in helping to amplify  his case that this is a fight for  the conservative party uh let alone  within british politics than the british  public itself so i think in any concept  of party leadership contest you are  going to see every single candidate  reaffirm their support for ukraine in  the ukrainian struggle and  there will almost certainly be a contest  over who can pledge the most money for  britain's armed forces  boris johnson was the leading light of  the campaign to get britain out of the  european union in 2016. he came to  office in 2019 on a pledge to get brexit  done to deliver the divorce that theresa  may could not and he has failed the  united kingdom has left the eu but the  the question of northern ireland uh and  that the common border that the united  kingdom and the republic of ireland  share has not been addressed now just  before he was leaving office he unveiled  a new plan under which the united  kingdom would unilaterally renounce the  the the protocol on northern ireland  which put arrangements in place to to  address that the new leader faces a  choice do they push on with that plan  which will um toxify relations with the  european union and amount to a breach of  international law or do they return to  diplomacy and trying to find an agreed  solution  boris johnson came to power pledging to  restore britain's place in the world and  end the humiliation that was the theresa  may period when the dea